Why would an animal's ability to speak like a human be an indication
that that animal had evolved somehow (taking for granted that
evolution means better for the creature)?  As it is, they seem to
understand English better than we understand whatever laguage they
speak, not only that, but they read human body language and moods more
fluently than humans do.  They might have to "tell" us something a
hundered times before we catch on.  Let's try to evolve our own
capacity to understand our own language - not just the plain old
verbal kind.  And rather than enhancing our pets with "THE WORD" (as
though our ability to understand them would mean that they had
evolved), let's enhance them in a way that will enable them to open
the damn door themselves.  
